    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "superimposition-source-for-dorian",
      "narrative": "Benson instructs that existing Cmaj7 and Fmaj7 arpeggio lines can be directly recycled as D Dorian vocabulary: 'by combining Cmaj7 lines with Fmaj7 lines, we can build a beautiful D dorian line. So, it means that we already have thousands of dorian lines just adapting the major 7th lines to minor chords' (Chapter 2, p. 145).",
