    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7b9",
      "function_role": "diminished-shape-selection-context-dependent",
      "narrative": "Benson rejects a rigid rule for which diminished fingering shape to choose: 'there is no rule about what shape is the best, because it will depend on what comes next in terms of melody. Therefore, the best thing to do is to memorize many single line ideas using the diminished chord' (Chapter 3, p. 248).",
      "source_principle_ids": [
