      "function_role": "exception-allowing-4th-as-target-tone",
      "narrative": "Benson carves out an explicit exception to the avoid-note rule for the 4th over a dominant: 'The only exception is when the chord is a Gsus, so the C note will work with this chord as a starting note or even an ending note' (Chapter 2, p. 144).",
