      "chord_quality": "min-maj7",
      "function_role": "resolution-note-must-respect-destination",
      "narrative": "Benson establishes that the ending note must always fit the tonic chord: 'always pay attention to the resolution note because we must always respect the ending chord, which in this case is Cm7, a non C harmonic minor scale chord. Actually, most of the time, the ending chord of a cadence V7/I will not be derived from the harmonic minor scale' (Chapter 3, p. 235).",
