      "function_role": "natural-6th-forbidden-over-v7-im-cadence",
      "narrative": "Benson forbids the natural 6th (A natural in C minor) in any line played over a V7-Im cadence: 'If we have the cadence G7, Cm7, we cannot use the A note (major 6th) to build single lines, because this note is derived from the dorian scale and cannot be played over any cadence' (Chapter 3, p. 261).",
